From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:17:38 +0200
Subject: Add the 2021 re-release's add-ons: Armagon, Dissolution, Dimensions
 of the Past, Dimension of the Machine

GOG's Quake Enhanced installer (setup_quake_enhanced_1.0_(60828).exe)
ships the re-release's own builds of the two mission packs and of
Dimensions of the Past: hipnotic/pak0.pak (79928896 bytes), rogue/pak0.pak
(44490612 bytes) and dopa/pak0.pak (40600041 bytes), each with a
progs.dat of its own written for the re-release (its strings, $qc_...,
come from the re-release's localization/loc_english.txt), and the mission
packs' music as Ogg Vorbis (hipnotic/music and rogue/music, track02-09;
not the quake_mp1/mp2_soundtrack.zip rips). Dimension of the Machine is
the mg1/pak0.pak gdp already knows. QuakeSpasm 0.94 and later play them
from the re-release's base directory with -game hipnotic, rogue, dopa or
mg1, so they are expansions of quake-rerelease in $assets/quake-rerelease,
not of quake-registered:

- quake-rerelease-armagon: hipnotic/pak0.pak, its music optional
- quake-rerelease-dissolution: rogue/pak0.pak, its music optional
- quake-rerelease-dopa: dopa/pak0.pak
- quake-rerelease-dimension-of-the-machine: mg1/pak0.pak

The installer's ctf/pak0.pak (Threewave CTF, multiplayer only) is not
packaged.

QuakeTask wrote hipnotic-tryexec.sh or rogue-tryexec.sh into
$assets/quake for any package installing a hipnotic or rogue file; that
detector is for the quake wrapper's mission pack launchers, which play
$assets/quake, so packages installed elsewhere no longer get one (it
would also clash with quake-armagon's and quake-dissolution's).

Forwarded: not yet (candidate for Debian)

